<% content_for :title, "Terms" %>
<% content_for :description, "The terms for using Yonderbook: a free tool, provided as is, for checking your reading list against your library." %>
<%# #1416. Plain language on purpose. Have a lawyer read it before relying on it. %>

<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
  <div class="mb-10">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight text-mauve-950 mb-3">Terms</h1>
    <p class="text-mauve-700">Last updated 10 November 2026</p>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-10 text-mauve-700 leading-relaxed">
    <section>
      <p>By using Yonderbook you agree to these terms. They're short because the service is simple: you give it a reading list, and it tells you what your library has.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-medium text-mauve-950 mb-3">The service</h2>
      <p>Yonderbook is free. It reads your Goodreads shelves or an export you upload, and checks them against libraries through OverDrive. Availability comes from OverDrive and changes constantly, so what we show can be out of date or wrong. Always confirm in Libby or your library's catalog before relying on it.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-medium text-mauve-950 mb-3">What you can upload</h2>
      <p class="mb-3">Upload only a Goodreads library export: your own, or one you have permission to use. Don't upload anything unlawful, anything that isn't a reading list, or anything meant to break or overload the service.</p>
      <p>What you upload is shown only to you. We don't publish it or share it with other users.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-medium text-mauve-950 mb-3">Using it fairly</h2>
      <p>Don't use Yonderbook to scrape OverDrive, Goodreads or BookMooch, to send automated traffic, or to get around the limits those services set. We may block access that does.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-medium text-mauve-950 mb-3">Other services</h2>
      <p>Goodreads, OverDrive, Libby, BookMooch and your library have their own terms, which apply when you use them through Yonderbook. We aren't affiliated with or endorsed by any of them, and features that depend on them can stop working if they change.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-medium text-mauve-950 mb-3">Your account</h2>
      <p>You don't need one. If you make one, keep your sign-in to yourself, and delete the account whenever you like from <a class="text-mauve-950 underline hover:no-underline" href="/account">Account</a>. We may remove accounts that break these terms. See <a class="text-mauve-950 underline hover:no-underline" href="/privacy">Privacy</a> for what an account stores.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-medium text-mauve-950 mb-3">No warranty</h2>
      <p>Yonderbook is provided as is, without warranties of any kind. It may be unavailable, slow or wrong, and it may change or stop entirely. To the extent the law allows, we aren't liable for any loss from using it or from relying on what it shows.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-medium text-mauve-950 mb-3">Changes and questions</h2>
      <p>If these terms change, we'll update this page and the date at the top. For questions, use the chat button in the corner of any page.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
